---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Unit from '../components/Unit.astro';
import { unitByMidi } from '../data/site';

const unit = unitByMidi.get(64)!;
---
<Base title="Measured in staff spaces" description={unit.description} note={unit.midi}>
  <Unit unit={unit}>
    <p class="lede" slot="lede" data-split="lines" data-intro data-delay="0.15">
      Everything on the staff is sized from one number: the gap between two staff lines.
    </p>
    <figure class="figure figure--spaces">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="spaces-title" focusable="false">
        <title id="spaces-title">A staff with one notehead and stem, measured in staff spaces</title>
        <g class="fig-staff">
          <line x1="120" y1="60" x2="620" y2="60" /><line x1="120" y1="84" x2="620" y2="84" />
          <line x1="120" y1="108" x2="620" y2="108" /><line x1="120" y1="132" x2="620" y2="132" />
          <line x1="120" y1="156" x2="620" y2="156" />
        </g>
        <text class="smufl fig-clef" x="132" y="132">{''}</text>
        <ellipse class="fig-ink" cx="400" cy="108" rx="15.6" ry="12" transform="rotate(-20.05 400 108)" />
        <line class="fig-stem" x1="414.6" y1="106" x2="414.6" y2="24" />
        <g class="fig-dim">
          <path data-draw pathLength="1" d="M96 60 V156 M90 60 H102 M90 156 H102" />
          <path data-draw pathLength="1" d="M300 84 V108 M294 84 H306 M294 108 H306" />
          <path data-draw pathLength="1" d="M384.4 184 H415.6 M384.4 178 V190 M415.6 178 V190" />
          <path data-draw pathLength="1" d="M440 24 V108 M434 24 H446 M434 108 H446" />
        </g>
        <g class="fig-label">
          <text x="84" y="112" text-anchor="end">4 spaces</text>
          <text x="288" y="100" text-anchor="end">1 space</text>
          <text x="400" y="210" text-anchor="middle">1.3 spaces</text>
          <text x="452" y="70">3.5 spaces</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>The staff is four spaces tall. A notehead is 1.3 spaces wide and one high; a stem is 3.5.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Noteheads lean about 20 degrees, the way engraved heads do. The clef is set at a font size of four
        spaces, and the time signature digits each fill two. Nothing on the staff has a fixed pixel size.
      </p>
      <p>
        That rule paid off later. When the app added a grand staff for two hands, it needed no new drawing
        code: a grand staff is two staves, each half the height, and every glyph scales with its own staff.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clefs, braces and time signatures come from Bravura, the reference font of the SMuFL music standard.
        Unicode clef characters fall back to whatever font the system has, sit at the wrong height, and are
        missing on some Android builds.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Unit>
</Base>
